Instrument FOV Definition(s)
----------------------------------------------------------

   This section defines the following FOVs:

      ID       SHAPE      FRAME          SIZE      BSIGHT  SOURCE
      -------  --------   -------------  --------  ------  -------------
      -64310   CIRCLE     ORX_OTES        0.229     +Z     Ivens, 09/24/13

   where the source means:

       Ivens          -- from John Ivens' e-mail(s)

   All sizes are half-extents given in degrees.

   The FOVs are defined in this data block.

   \begindata

      INS-64310_FOV_CLASS_SPEC       = 'ANGLES'
      INS-64310_FOV_SHAPE            = 'CIRCLE'
      INS-64310_FOV_FRAME            = 'ORX_OTES'
      INS-64310_BORESIGHT            = ( 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 )
      INS-64310_FOV_REF_VECTOR       = ( 1.0, 0.0, 0.0 )
      INS-64310_FOV_REF_ANGLE        = ( 0.229 )
      INS-64310_FOV_ANGLE_UNITS      = ( 'DEGREES' )

   \begintext

End of the IK file.
